  "title": "As the Ratchet Turns",
  "summary": "Stocks are starting the new month off with a bang. Oil futures are lower after the President called off a promised round of strikes on Iran, saying that, “There’s a deal on Hormuz, and then there will be a deal on the nuclear or you might call it the denuclearization of Iran.” Oil futures traded sharply lower, bringing bond yields along with them. The Japanese yen held at stronger levels after bilateral intervention by the US and Japan. And the rally in megacap tech, along with pretty much everything else, continued.",
